  "id": "Compound::DB01026 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Ketoconazole is linked to Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the broader class of azole compounds. The evidence suggests that Ketoconazole, as an azole, binds to Cyp2c19 through a shared pathway involving the inclusion of azoles in the category of Anti-Infective Agents and Organic Aromatic Compounds. This implies that the mechanism of action may involve the inhibition of Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is a common target for many drugs. The presence of multiple azole derivatives, such as Luliconazole and Oxiconazole, which also bind to Cyp2c19, further supports the notion that the interaction is not unique to Ketoconazole but is a broader property of the azole class. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for azole compounds to modulate Cyp2c19 activity, which could be relevant in drug development and pharmacogenomics.",
